    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-floor offensive profile, anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), both of whom benefit from prime matchups against mediocre right-handed pitching. **Jackson Merrill** is a focal point of our strategy; despite a slight penalty for facing a catcher with a quick pop time, his efficiency against Littell makes him our top-scoring option. **Kyle Tucker** (74.37) rounds out our elite tier, utilizing a favorable wind and a mid-order slot to capitalize on Painter\u2019s middling xERA. We are also monitoring **Gunnar Henderson** (71.72), whose score remains remarkably robust despite drawing a difficult matchup against Miles (2.95 xERA); his explosive park factors and lineup placement allow him to transcend the elite SP disadvantage.\n\n**Sam Antonacci** (61.66) and **Josh Jung** (60.61) provide solid production as we round out the starting lineup. **Sam Antonacci** was a key riser, leveraging a high xwOBA (0.379) and a leadoff advantage to secure his start, while **Josh Jung** remains a staple in the lineup due to neutral platoon stability. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.95) narrowly missed the \"Strong\" start threshold; he remains our most interesting bench-adjacent player. While his park factors are excellent, the defensive skill of Bradish created a drag on his efficiency, forcing him into a UTIL slot that sits just below the aggressive 60+ threshold. **Liam Hicks** (43.12) and **Brayan Rocchio** (43.08) are our most fragile starts today, largely suppressed by unfavorable SP matchups and bottom-of-the-order hitting positions; they are active, but represent our primary candidates for cap preservation if early innings trend poorly.\n\nThe depth of the roster remains compromised by the injury bug, with **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Drake Baldwin** all confirmed as unavailable. We are continuing to track the recovery timelines of reserves like **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Miguel Andujar**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Dominic Smith** to see if any can provide necessary relief for our bench. As of now, weather conditions appear stable, but with **Liam Hicks** and **Gunnar Henderson** facing sub-3.10 xERA pitchers, we will be watching early exit velocity numbers closely to ensure these starters aren't neutralized by high-end command.",
